<title>SWITZERLAND: Holderbank 1996 profit falls on provisions.</title>
<headline>Holderbank 1996 profit falls on provisions.</headline>
<dateline>GLARUS, Switzerland 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calender 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p>Group net before provisions</p>
<p> and valuation adjustment   646		 vs 611</p>
<p> Provisions,value adjustm.  450		 vs zero</p>
<p>Net profit after provisions</p>
<p> and valuation adjustment   196		 vs 611</p>
<p>Attributable earnings, i.e.</p>
<p> after minorities	     43		  vs 450</p>
<p>Note - Full name is Holderbank Financire Glarus AG</p>
<p> Dividend, Sfr, bearer	17		  vs 17</p>
<p> Dividend, Sfr, registered  3.40		vs 3.40</p>
<p> Net sales			9,951	     vs 8,270</p>
<p> Gross profit		   3,552	     vs 3,005</p>
<p> Operating profit	     1,103	     vs 1,113</p>
<p>Sales volume of cement</p>
<p> and clinker in million tonnes: 62.3	  vs 53.5</p>
<p> Aggregate sales		73.3		vs 73.4</p>
<p>Ready-mixed concrete, cubic</p>
<p> metres			   18.2		vs 16.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Holderbank said in a statement that it had revised 1995 results to reflect International Accounting Standards (IAS). Holderbank originally reported a 1995 net profit of 629 million francs.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
